    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d156">

                <pb facs="0192" n="182" sameAs="frus:frus1942China/pg182"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 G 231/582: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-12-04T11:00:00+07:00">December 4,
                            1942—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1430. In a friendly private conversation with me yesterday afternoon Foreign
                    Minister Soong on his own initiative referred to an article regarding me in
                    Washington Merry-Go-Round of October 28,<anchor n="50" xml:id="d156-f1"/> which
                    he described as “clumsy propaganda” and said that the article had come to the
                    notice of the Generalissimo who had desired Soong to tell me that the statements
                    in the article regarding Chiang’s attitude toward me were entirely untrue.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d156-f1" n="50" xml:id="d156-f1-content">
                <p>Drew Pearson had reported that it was an inescapable fact that Generalissimo
                    Chiang Kai-shek did not like Ambassador Gauss and would like to have him
                    replaced.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
